function update(a, b) {
```

The initial global declarations are:

```
x = 3;
y = 2;
z = 5;
```

I'll use the header and global declarations to determine which LHSs are parameters vs. globals by identifying that `a` and `b` are local parameters because they are listed in the function header, and `x`, `y`, and `z` are global variables because they are declared outside the function.

I'll use the copy-back phrase to handle value-result cases by ensuring that any changes made to the parameters inside the function are reflected back to the original variables in the left-to-right order, which will affect my work on part (b) by making sure that the changes to `x` and `z` are directly applied to the global variables.

